From 697f598eb301250dffab1d1405a81afcbd6bcc14 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Medium1992 <Medium1992@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 16:08:04 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] XHTTP: Add "h2Flow": {"queueCuts": false}, which leaves the
 path's queue to TCP

A governed server cuts its downloads against the queue it sees on the path, which holds that queue short, at the cost of giving way to traffic that keeps it full. An inbound that carries bridges, or that would rather keep its share than its latency, can now turn that off: pi and the cut at a long queue do not run, and the downloads' windows follow their readers alone. Beside four other flows for 20 seconds a download then averages 36 Mbit/s, as without a governor, where the default gets 20; the request beside eight downloads takes 150-265 ms where the default takes 65.
